#!/usr/bin/env sh
# pre-push — two mechanical gates before a push reaches prod:
#   1. MONEY SMOKE  (runs when server/ changed) — the money-path test suites
#      against an isolated Neon ci-smoke branch (scripts/testdb-smoke.js).
#      Runs FIRST because it fails faster than the ~1 min client build.
#   2. CLIENT BUILD (runs when client/ changed) — the EXACT command Vercel runs
#      (CI=true react-scripts build), where ESLint warnings are FATAL. Nothing
#      else local catches that: lint-staged only covers server/, and a plain
#      `eslint` run treats it as a non-fatal warning.
#
# Both now live in scripts/push-gate.js so the hook and `npm run gate` can
# never drift, and so a gate that ALREADY passed for this exact tree is not
# re-run here. That re-run is what was breaking pushes: git opens the SSH
# connection before this hook runs, so an 8-minute hook left the connection
# idle until GitHub closed it, and the push then failed after passing
# everything (2026-08-14; see the header in scripts/push-gate.js).
#
# Fail-closed is unchanged, and the receipt is only honoured when ALL of these
# hold: same HEAD, byte-identical content for every modified/untracked file,
# under 12h old, covering the gates this push needs, and the sha being pushed
# IS HEAD (both gates test the WORKING TREE, so they cannot vouch for
# `git push origin <other-sha>:main`). Anything else and the full gate runs
# right here exactly as it always did.
#
# TWO PATHS, and the flip marker decides (instruction rewrite step 3; spec
# 2026-10-19 sections 4.3 and 8). push-gate.js verify reads
# <git-common-dir>/drb-flip.json first:
#   - absent (today, and for the flip push itself): the fingerprint receipt
#     path described above, unchanged, the markers unread.
#   - present: the hook validates only and never runs a gate, so nothing slow
#     happens inside git's SSH window. For a push to refs/heads/main only (any
#     other remote ref is refused), it refuses on a standing gate or watch
#     marker, then checks each pushed sha's sha receipt
#     (<git-common-dir>/drb-gate/<sha>.json, written by
#     push-gate.js sha, which ship calls) against origin/main, then the review
#     receipts over origin/main..<sha>. No receipt means refuse with
#     "run npm run ship".
#   - unreadable: refuse until the file is repaired or removed by hand.
# Emergencies only, visible and per-push: git push --no-verify, or HUSKY=0.
set -e

node scripts/push-gate.js verify
